                <h1 class="content-title">Walk-up Experience & <span class="gradient-text">CIM</span></h1>
                <p class="content-subtitle">
                    Master onsite Tech Lounge support with Walk-up Experience (kiosks, queue management, stockroom integration) 
                    and enterprise service optimization with Continual Improvement Management (CIM).
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Section 1: Walk-up Mission -->
            <section class="content-section" id="walkup-mission">
                <h2>Walk-up Experience: The In-Person Tech Lounge</h2>
                <p>
                    The <strong>Walk-up Experience</strong> brings the consumer-grade "Genius Bar / Tech Lounge" support model into 
                    the enterprise office. Employees visit an onsite IT service desk for face-to-face hardware troubleshooting, 
                    device upgrades, and instant peripheral replacements.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Rather than waiting in disorganized physical queues, the Walk-up application manages digital check-ins, 
                    appointment scheduling, live wait-time estimates on public displayboards, and automated technician routing.
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Self-Service Check-In Kiosk</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Touchscreen tablets or badge readers at the lounge entrance allow users to scan corporate badges, 
                            select their issue category, and enter the digital queue with real-time SMS updates.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Online Appointment Booking</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Requesters reserve 15-minute support slots in advance via Employee Center or mobile app, 
                            guaranteeing dedicated technician availability without office wait time.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Live Queue Displayboard</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Wall-mounted TV monitors display currently served tickets, upcoming queue positions, and estimated wait times 
                            in real time.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 2: Walk-up Schema & Architecture -->
            <section class="content-section" id="walkup-schema">
                <h2>Walk-up Table Architecture & Schema</h2>
                <p>
                    The Walk-up data model extends the Interaction framework to track visitors, wait times, and fulfillment:
                </p>

                <table class="data-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Table Name</th>
                            <th>Parent Extension</th>
                            <th>Operational Scope</th>
                            <th>Key Columns</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>wu_location</code></td>
                            <td><code>cmn_location</code></td>
                            <td>Physical Tech Lounge locations (e.g. Building 4 Tech Bar).</td>
                            <td><code>name</code>, <code>schedule</code>, <code>capacity</code>, <code>manager</code></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>wu_queue</code></td>
                            <td>None (Base Table)</td>
                            <td>Location queue configuration and service offerings.</td>
                            <td><code>location</code>, <code>max_wait_time</code>, <code>estimated_service_duration</code></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>wu_interaction</code></td>
                            <td><code>interaction</code></td>
                            <td>Individual visitor session record.</td>
                            <td>
                                <code>guest</code> (Ref to <code>sys_user</code>), <code>wu_queue</code>, <code>check_in_time</code>, 
                                <code>wait_time</code>, <code>service_time</code>, <code>state</code> (Queued, Serving, Closed)
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>wu_appointment</code></td>
                            <td><code>sn_apptmnt_booking_appointment_booking</code></td>
                            <td>Scheduled calendar reservations.</td>
                            <td><code>location</code>, <code>start_date_time</code>, <code>end_date_time</code>, <code>profile</code></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <div class="diagram-block">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Walk-up Visitor Journey & Fulfillment Flow</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    graph TD
                        VISIT["Employee Arrives at Tech Lounge or Books Online"] --> CHECKIN["Kiosk Badge Scan / Appointment Check-In"]
                        
                        CHECKIN --> QUEUED["wu_interaction Inserted (state = Queued)<br>Displayboard updates & SMS sent with queue number"]
                        
                        QUEUED --> TECH["Technician Workbench Alerts Agent via SOW / AWA"]
                        TECH --> ACCEPT["Agent Clicks 'Serve Next'<br>wu_interaction state = Serving"]
                        
                        ACCEPT --> ACTION{"Diagnostic Assessment"}
                        ACTION -->|Quick Fix / Peripheral| DISPO["Issue Consumable / Loaner Laptop<br>Direct HAM Stockroom deduction"]
                        ACTION -->|Complex Hardware Defect| INC["Promote Interaction to Incident / RITM<br>Device retained for repair"]
                        
                        DISPO --> CLOSE["Complete Session (wu_interaction closed)<br>Customer survey dispatched"]
                        INC --> CLOSE
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 3: Stockroom Integration -->
            <section class="content-section" id="stockroom-integration">
                <h2>Stockroom & Loaner Asset Management Integration</h2>
                <p>
                    Walk-up lounges connect directly to <strong>Hardware Asset Management (HAM)</strong> stockrooms:
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Consumable Disposables</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Cables, USB-C hubs, power adapters, and mice (<code>alm_consumable</code>) are issued with a single click, 
                            instantly decrementing stockroom inventory counts.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Loaner Laptop Checkout</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Temporary loaner assets (<code>alm_hardware</code>) are scanned and assigned to the user with automated return 
                            due dates and overdue reminder notifications.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 4: CIM Framework -->
            <section class="content-section" id="cim-framework">
                <h2>Continual Improvement Management (CIM)</h2>
                <p>
                    According to ITIL v4, the purpose of <strong>Continual Improvement</strong> is to 
                    <em>"align the organization's practices and services with changing business needs through the ongoing identification 
                    and improvement of services, service components, practices, or any element involved in the management of services."</em>
                </p>
                <p>
                    The <strong>CIM application (`sn_cim`)</strong> provides an enterprise framework to register, prioritize, 
                    and track structured improvement initiatives across ITSM, DevOps, and IT operations.
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>1. Where are we now?</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Baselines current operational performance using Performance Analytics indicators 
                            (e.g., <em>"Average P1 MTTR is currently 6.2 hours"</em>).
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>2. Where do we want to be?</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Defines measurable target KPIs and strategic business goals 
                            (e.g., <em>"Reduce P1 MTTR to under 2.5 hours by Q4"</em>).
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>3. How do we get there?</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Decomposes initiatives into executable tasks (<code>sn_cim_task</code>) linked to Change Requests, 
                            Agile Development Stories, or training programs.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 5: CIM Register Schema -->
            <section class="content-section" id="cim-register">
                <h2>CIM Improvement Register Schema</h2>
                <p>
                    The Continual Improvement Register centralizes all enhancement proposals across the enterprise:
                </p>

                <table class="data-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Table Name</th>
                            <th>Parent Extension</th>
                            <th>Operational Scope</th>
                            <th>Key Columns</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>sn_cim_register</code></td>
                            <td><code>task</code></td>
                            <td>Master Continual Improvement Initiative record.</td>
                            <td>
                                <code>short_description</code>, <code>business_case</code>, <code>strategic_objective</code>, 
                                <code>kpi</code> (Ref to <code>pa_indicators</code>), <code>target_value</code>, <code>actual_value</code>, 
                                <code>state</code> (Draft, Assessment, In Progress, Complete)
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>sn_cim_task</code></td>
                            <td><code>task</code></td>
                            <td>Individual execution milestones and work packages.</td>
                            <td><code>initiative</code> (Ref to <code>sn_cim_register</code>), <code>assigned_to</code>, <code>state</code></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>sn_cim_m2m_initiative_task</code></td>
                            <td>None (Base M2M)</td>
                            <td>Links initiatives to originating Incidents, Problems, or Audits.</td>
                            <td><code>initiative</code>, <code>task</code></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 6: KPI & Strategy Alignment -->
            <section class="content-section" id="kpi-alignment">
                <h2>KPI Alignment & Automated Validation</h2>
                <p>
                    CIM initiatives link directly to <strong>Performance Analytics (PA)</strong> indicators:
                </p>
                <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                    <li><strong>Real-Time Scorecard Tracking:</strong> As resolver teams implement process optimizations, the linked PA indicator dynamically tracks whether the target metric is being achieved.</li>
                    <li><strong>Post-Improvement Validation:</strong> When an initiative moves to <em>Complete</em>, the system monitors the indicator for 90 days to confirm that improvements are sustained over time.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

